WEBVTT

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:14.530
RULES OF THE PRETTY BOY DETECTIVE CLUB
1. BE PRETTY. 2. BE A BOY. 3. BE A DETECTIVE.

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:20.040
For a speech, it's not what
was said that's important,
but who had said it.
--Unknown

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:54.550
ZASHIKI-WARASHI

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:59.050
'A
 ZASHIKI-WARASHI CAME 
WALKING TOWARDS ME'

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:28.330
'BEAUTIFUL'

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:35.090
'NOT A SINGLE SOUND OF A FOOTSTEP'

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:41.090
'LIKE A PEONY STANDING, 
LIKE A TREE PEONY
SITTING, 
AND LIKE A LILY WALKING'

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:43.100
YURIKA (TEMPORARY NAME)

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:50.350
'WHY IS THERE A GIRL IN 
TRADITIONAL JAPANESE
CLOTHING AT A MIDDLE
 SCHOOL CAMPUS?'

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:08.920
Move, impoverished.
You want to get run over and die?

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.000
'WHAT?'

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.000
'WHAT DID SHE SAY? JUST NOW?'

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:16.300
I said move. Do you want to die?

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:21.050
What's a peasant doing
standing on their legs in front of me?

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.640
'HUH? SHOULD I 
NOT BE STANDING?'

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:29.310
This is why mortals are so...

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:35.280
When I think about having to rule over ilk
like this, it makes me want to kill myself.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:39.490
As for you, I've remembered your face now.

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:42.160
'LIKE A PEONY STANDING,
 LIKE A TREE PEONY SITTING, 
AND LIKE A LILY WALKING'

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:46.160
'AND THE UTTERED WORDS
 WERE ROSE THORNS'

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:50.660
MICHIRU
 FUKUROI

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.710
What are you standing there for, Mayumi?

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:55.760
Oh, Mr. Delinquent!

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:55.420
MAYUMI 
DOJIMA

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:59.130
Something wrong with you?
What happened?

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:03.810
I didn't think I would feel so at ease
by seeing your savage face.

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:07.350
I'd like to apologize how I've always
thought about wanting to frustrate you.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:13.150
Then apologize right now. For starters,
apologize how you just said "savage face."

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:18.320
Oh by the way, Mr. Delinquent,
do you think Sakiguchi will be coming today?

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:21.780
Oh, Nagahiro? I don't know.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:25.450
What, you wanted something from Nagahiro?

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:29.000
Well, his attendance is rather terrible.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:33.290
It's only normal this time of year
because he's busy with student council work.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:39.090
Anyway, how long will you distance yourself
from Nagahiro by calling him "Sakiguchi"?

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:43.470
"Mr. Delinquent," "Mr. Bare-Legs,"
and top that off with "Mr. Genius."

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:49.020
You gave us all terrible nicknames, but why
do you only call Nagahiro by his proper name?

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:53.110
I-I mean, well, Sakiguchi is a third-year.

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:56.650
I can't just call an upperclassman
"Lolicon dude," you know?

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:59.320
I'm not saying you should go that far.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:01.610
There's no upperclassman or underclassman.

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:07.200
The Pretty Boy Detective Club just has our
leader at the top, and we operate as a group.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:09.330
Everyone under him is equal.

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:13.790
Otherwise, there's no way I'd be doing anything
together with someone like Nagahiro.

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:20.090
So Mayumi, if Nagahiro is around today,

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:23.760
and you have something you want to talk
to him about, it'll be a good opportunity.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:26.600
Call him maybe "Mr. President" starting today.

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:31.890
Mr. President? But if I called him that,
wouldn't he catch on that I'm making fun of him?

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:34.560
So you do fundamentally make fun of him.

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:49.450
It was a giant <i>hagoita</i>.

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:51.780
OSHIE-HAGOITA

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:56.040
Apparently it's called an "<i>oshie-hagoita</i>."

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:59.460
Maybe it's a new artistic piece
that Sosaku created?

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:00.920
SOSAKU 
YUBIWA

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:03.130
He doesn't recall anything like that.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:03.050
MANABU 
SOTOIN

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:05.800
Then is it another one of Ms. Towai's pieces?

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:08.470
That can't be, Mayumi.

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:12.100
Towai is an outsider to this academy now.

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:16.230
How would she set up
such a suspicious object in the art room?

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:15.680
HYOTA
ASHIKAGA

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:19.940
He's definitely right about that.

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:24.200
Maybe it's that con artist.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:29.790
There's just too little merit or returns
to theorize that he was the perpetrator.

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:36.210
Fudatsuki is a gambler,
so he would prioritize how amusing it is.

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:40.170
You seem to understand
that shady guy a whole lot.

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:42.050
Oh, that's not it, Mr. Delinquent.

00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:44.590
It's just that knowing your enemy
and knowing yourself

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:45.930
makes you unafraid of a hundred battles.

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:47.090
Don't get jealous, okay?

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:50.930
Who would be?
You really don't know yourself at all, do you?

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:53.390
Yeah, it's not really like him.

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:58.270
The boldness of sending a gift
into enemy territory is truly being a gambler,

00:06:58.270 --> 00:07:02.030
but in this case, it doesn't make sense
to send in a <i>hagoita</i>.

00:07:02.030 --> 00:07:05.610
There's nothing as meaningless as a playful
heart that doesn't get its message across.

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:09.410
What are you talking about?
Isn't it crystal clear?

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:12.490
It's because it's almost the new year.

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:14.960
What about the "Twenties"?

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:17.170
Can this be something Rei could've done?

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:20.920
That's a possibility
that can be immediately dismissed.

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:25.840
Because the "Twenties" led by Rei
is an actual criminal syndicate.

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:32.010
It's one thing if the <i>hagoita </i>was wire-tapped
or had a bomb planted on it.

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:35.890
But I've already confirmed that
to not to be the case with my own eyes.

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:37.440
That's too bad.

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:41.520
What a shame. I thought
I could see those plump legs again.

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:47.110
What, so in the end we don't know anything,
and we have no likely suspects?

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:49.780
Then it's useless to be debating about it.

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:52.740
Why don't we have Nagahiro
investigate this then?

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:53.830
I see.

00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:58.040
Indeed, this is probably as far as
we can discuss things without Nagahiro.

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:01.290
Then, let's move on to the next topic at hand.

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:02.960
It's almost winter break,

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:06.920
so I was thinking of holding a winter
training camp for the Pretty Boy Detective Club.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:08.970
We moved on really quickly.

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:13.720
I don't think this matter is something
that can be so easily shelved.

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:17.230
If there were only a witness who saw
a suspicious individual

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:19.600
bringing in a suspicious object.

00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:22.360
That's right.

00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:28.280
In visiting this art room today,
I had crossed paths with a <i>yokai</i>.

00:08:28.280 --> 00:08:34.030
Maybe that<i> zashiki-warashi</i>
was on its way back from the art room?

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:37.450
Then, that little one is the culprit?

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:42.580
Was that child the suspicious individual who
brought a suspicious object into the art room?

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:44.550
A winter training camp?

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:46.340
What's up with that, Leader?

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:49.680
Are we going to coop ourselves
in some villa in the snowy mountains?

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:52.180
Do you intend to make me
cook all three meals?

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:55.100
You know how much effort that is?

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:57.980
I'm not your personal chef, you know.

00:08:57.980 --> 00:09:02.940
I can't afford to not show up to team practice
at all during winter break,

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:05.610
so I'd like you to adjust the schedule a bit.

00:09:05.610 --> 00:09:10.950
And though I'm bracing myself for it,
can you avoid really cold places?

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:15.580
If I get goosebumps,
it would ruin my beautiful legs.

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:18.540
Um... Can I say something?

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:20.540
What is it, Mayumi?

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:24.500
If you have requests for the winter
training camp, let's hear them.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:27.500
Not that.
It's about the case with the <i>hagoita</i>.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:29.010
Oh my, what's this?

00:09:29.010 --> 00:09:32.130
You're still wondering about that?
You're quite fixated on it, aren't you?

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:37.890
What is it, Mayumi? You look like you've been
wanting to say something for a while.

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:39.810
Zashiki-warashi.

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:44.020
I saw a<i> zashiki-warashi </i>on my way here.

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:46.730
Perhaps that little one was the culprit

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:51.490
who brought in that creepy <i>oshie-hagoita</i>
into the art room.

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:58.040
Mayumi.

00:09:58.040 --> 00:10:03.080
Did that thing call you something like
"impoverished" or "peasant"

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:06.790
or "uninformed" or "scum of society"?

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:08.460
W-Well...

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:12.090
I think I was called
"impoverished" and "peasant."

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:14.800
I wasn't called
"uninformed" or "scum of society."

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:18.060
I think there was one other term...

00:10:18.060 --> 00:10:23.270
It was so horrifying that I conveniently
cut it out of my memory, it seems.

00:10:23.270 --> 00:10:24.810
It was "mortals," right?

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:27.440
Why is this? Why do they know?

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:27.140
MORTALS

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:31.360
Mr. Delinquent and Mr. Bare-Legs,
you know about Yurika?

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:33.780
That's no "Yurika."

00:10:33.780 --> 00:10:37.700
That child's name is Kodaki Kawaike.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:37.650
KODAKI KAWAIKE

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:39.700
She's Nagahiro's fiancée.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:44.370
It's probably suitable
to not call her a <i>yokai</i>, but a devil.

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:46.380
D-Devil?

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:52.210
Mayumi, it looks like a fearsome monster
has set her eyes on you.

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:53.670
KODAKI KAWAIKESECRET 
MISSION (ERRAND)

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:57.010
A lot went on before you joined, Mayumi.

00:10:57.010 --> 00:10:59.720
To be specific,
it was during the summer training camp.

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:01.220
Summer training camp?

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:05.690
No, to be more precise,
we didn't hold a summer training camp.

00:11:05.690 --> 00:11:08.560
We were forced to cancel it
thanks to the devil.

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:10.480
What the heck happened?

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:15.820
Let's see. What happened then
should be told by the actual person involved.

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:19.160
We've reached a point where the story
won't stand without Nagahiro.

00:11:19.160 --> 00:11:20.450
Mayumi.

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:23.870
I'm sorry, but can I ask you to run an errand?

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:34.960
NAGAHIRO
SAKIGUCHI

00:11:38.720 --> 00:11:41.050
Thank you for waiting, Miss Mayumi.

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:43.890
So, is something the matter?

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:49.230
I see. So that's what happened.

00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:53.070
I'm sorry that my fiancée
has troubled you, Miss Mayumi.

00:11:53.070 --> 00:11:55.820
Though this marriage was arranged
by our parents without consultation,

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:59.160
it would've been better if I introduced you
to her in a more proper manner.

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:00.530
Sure.

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:07.080
To say the conclusion first, that crime
was most definitely carried out by Miss Kodaki.

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:11.380
I believe her intent can also be explained,
by and large.

00:12:12.800 --> 00:12:17.800
Before you joined the club, Miss Mayumi,
various things had happened.

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:22.930
With that said, I thought everything
had settled down for now.

00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:26.430
However, when you joined the club,

00:12:26.430 --> 00:12:32.940
I did get worried that she would cause
some sort of trouble once again.

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:34.940
Because...

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:37.360
Because she...

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:42.240
Miss Kodaki Kawaike, class 1-A
in Yubiwa Academy Elementary School,

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:48.210
was denied entry into the Pretty Boy Detective
Club by none other than the leader himself.

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:52.290
As he mentioned a specific name,

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:56.880
that information was whispered
into my ear in a hushed manner.

00:12:56.880 --> 00:13:01.550
But none of it really sank into my brain.

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:08.640
U-Um, Sakiguchi.

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:13.810
You might be surprised
if I say something like this so suddenly.

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:16.480
But I can't hold it back anymore.

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:18.900
It has to be you, Sakiguchi.

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:22.740
Can you please listen to what I have to say?

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:23.820
Huh?

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:27.330
Does this sound like
I'm confessing my love to him?

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:28.580
No, that's not it!

00:13:28.580 --> 00:13:32.880
Sakiguchi, you truly are handsome,
but you're not my type at all!

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:36.380
Why does it sound like I was just dumped?

00:13:36.380 --> 00:13:39.590
There's something
I want you to teach me, Sakiguchi.

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:42.510
Um, it's about voices.

00:13:42.510 --> 00:13:44.010
Voices?

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:45.890
The choir contest.

00:13:45.890 --> 00:13:49.060
It's an established event in
Yubiwa Academy at the end of each year.

00:13:49.060 --> 00:13:52.100
The problem was how they split up the parts.

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:54.520
LOAFERS FOR BOYS

00:13:54.440 --> 00:14:00.610
I never gave an explanation about why I've been
attending school wearing a boy's uniform,

00:13:54.770 --> 00:13:55.770
SLACKS FOR BOYS

