00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:09.750
That's what was decided.

00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:10.910
And so...

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:15.000
Sakiguchi, can you teach me
how to change my vocal type?

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:19.000
So that I can vocalize tones low enough
to sing one song without feeling out of place.

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:22.170
Don't "And so" me.

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:26.970
You should ask the class rep or vice-rep
and have yourself reassigned to a soprano again.

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:32.180
I don't want to accidentally disclose
the existence of the Club when I talk to them.

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:34.850
That is indeed true, but...

00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:37.610
Well, very well.

00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:42.650
Since it seems like I've troubled you
with Miss Kodaki's case...

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:46.820
I will teach you techniques
so you can somehow manage to sing.

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:50.080
However, it's on one condition.

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:54.620
Condition?

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:57.840
Did he say unconditionally?

00:14:57.840 --> 00:15:04.550
Miss Mayumi, this must be some kind of fate,
so can you become friends with Miss Kodaki?

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:07.390
She doesn't have any friends.

00:15:07.390 --> 00:15:08.800
Come again?

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:11.810
But I don't have any friends either.

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:14.850
ALL SIX MEMBERS GATHER

00:15:16.440 --> 00:15:18.150
What do you think, Nagahiro?

00:15:18.150 --> 00:15:20.650
Is that one of Kodaki's pieces?

00:15:20.650 --> 00:15:22.820
Without a doubt, yes.

00:15:22.820 --> 00:15:27.200
As always, I have no idea
what she was attempting to create.

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:32.490
Perhaps this monster
is an imagery of her inner landscape?

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:34.960
Hello, Leader. I'm sorry I'm late.

00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:38.040
And I'm terribly sorry that my
personal matters are troubling you.

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:42.760
Oh no, I don't mind. There're no such things
as personal matters among us.

00:15:42.760 --> 00:15:47.220
We should all deal
with this pressing matter together.

00:15:50.350 --> 00:15:52.010
Perhaps Yurika...

00:15:52.010 --> 00:15:56.560
I mean, Kodaki wanted to be welcomed
into the Pretty Boy Detective Club,

00:15:56.560 --> 00:16:00.860
and left this <i>hagoita </i>here
as a resume of some kind?

00:16:00.860 --> 00:16:04.780
That's quite a kind way
to look at things, Miss Mayumi.

00:16:04.780 --> 00:16:07.610
I don't think that's the case, either.

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:11.620
Though I'd be in agreement
if you said it was a declaration of war.

00:16:11.620 --> 00:16:14.160
A declaration of war.

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:19.460
No wait, if I recall, the meaning behind
sending a <i>hagoita </i>to someone was...

00:16:19.460 --> 00:16:24.760
No matter what intent she had in leaving this
while all of us were not here,

00:16:24.760 --> 00:16:27.930
unfortunately we cannot ignore this.

00:16:27.930 --> 00:16:32.100
Though, it would be best
if she took this back herself.

00:16:32.100 --> 00:16:37.430
It would be only appropriate for her to admit
to her crime, and take responsibility for it.

00:16:37.430 --> 00:16:41.770
I don't think that shrewd devil
would listen honestly to what we have to say.

00:16:41.770 --> 00:16:43.570
It'll be fine, Michiru.

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:46.070
I have a great idea that addresses that point.

00:16:46.070 --> 00:16:51.820
I can't help but feel that I'm a part of this
so-called great idea.

00:16:51.820 --> 00:16:56.620
Right. We probably need to have Nagahiro
do the negotiation for us.

00:16:56.620 --> 00:17:01.630
We need you to ask one of the very few people
your beautiful voice doesn't work against,

00:17:01.630 --> 00:17:03.420
but I'll leave it to you.

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:09.300
I hate to say this in its stead,
but we should think about something else.

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:12.760
That <i>hagoita </i>is a size
that isn't easy to dispose of.

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:17.350
So how in the world did that devil
bring it inside this art room?

00:17:17.350 --> 00:17:23.480
If we can't figure this out, who knows
what she'll bring at what timing in the future.

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:27.900
For all we know, it may not be simply
a suspicious object, but a dangerous object.

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:30.270
KODAKI KAWAIKE'S

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:30.270
IMPOSSIBLE CRIME (CRIMINALITY)

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:30.270
PART 1

00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:34.490
You think so?
I don't think it's all that strange.

00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:36.910
She probably used a cart or something, right?

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:41.000
She couldn't use a cart.
This campus is full of staircases.

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:46.420
Even if she somehow resolved that issue, since
she brought the <i>hagoita </i>into the art room,

00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:51.380
Yurika would need
to take the cart back with her.

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:56.350
But when she crossed paths with me,
the<i> zashiki-warashi </i>was empty-handed.

00:17:56.350 --> 00:17:57.260
How's that?

00:17:57.260 --> 00:18:01.310
Why do you get in such high spirits
when you criticize other people's theories?

00:18:01.310 --> 00:18:04.100
Your personality is almost a complete match
with Kodaki Kawaike.

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:08.440
She asked someone to carry it here.
That wouldn't be a possibility, right?

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:10.190
KODAKI KAWAIKE'S

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:10.190
IMPOSSIBLE CRIME (CRIMINALITY)

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:10.190
PART 2

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:13.910
Even if the possibility exists,
considering the devil's personality,

00:18:13.910 --> 00:18:15.820
it'd be impossible for her to ask someone else.

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:17.200
KODAKI KAWAIKE'S

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:17.200
IMPOSSIBLE CRIME (CRIMINALITY)

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:17.200
PART 3

00:18:17.330 --> 00:18:21.500
Besides, psychologically she wouldn't want
to make herself more easily found

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:24.080
by increasing the number
of actual perpetrators.

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:28.000
Then does that mean Yurika isn't the culprit?

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:31.630
No, there's no doubt that she's the culprit.

00:18:31.630 --> 00:18:39.140
As I mentioned earlier, that <i>hagoita </i>is most
definitely a piece created by Miss Kodaki.

00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:44.980
There are currently
two mysteries that we must face.

00:18:44.980 --> 00:18:47.860
Why did Kodaki do such a thing?

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:48.810
PART 1

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:48.810
WHY DID KODAKI DO SUCH A THING?

00:18:48.940 --> 00:18:51.860
PART 2

00:18:48.940 --> 00:18:51.860
HOW DID KODAKI DO SUCH A THING?

00:18:49.150 --> 00:18:51.280
And how did Kodaki do such a thing?

00:18:51.280 --> 00:18:56.030
Nagahiro will approach her personally
for the unclear motive,

00:18:56.030 --> 00:19:03.330
and we can think about how it becomes strange
if the devil is the culprit.

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:07.460
Well, the first thing that comes to mind
is instead of bringing in the completed item,

00:19:07.460 --> 00:19:13.260
but bring in the components in small bits
and pieces and build it in the art room.

00:19:13.260 --> 00:19:16.090
Um, that's impossible, Mr. Delinquent.

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:18.890
That thing is one solid board.

00:19:18.890 --> 00:19:25.690
That <i>hagoita </i>is completed in that shape, and
of a size that no child could possibly carry.

00:19:25.690 --> 00:19:29.230
In the first place, can you fit something
of that size through the door?

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:32.740
And maybe it's surprisingly hollow
and really light?

00:19:32.740 --> 00:19:34.530
Picking up the <i>hagoita</i>

00:19:34.530 --> 00:19:41.450
and seeing if it fits through the door
would kill two birds with one stone.

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:44.960
The question is, who would do it?

00:19:44.960 --> 00:19:49.170
Who's going to touch that eerie <i>hagoita</i>?

00:19:49.170 --> 00:19:54.420
The least powerful member of the Club
should do this job.

00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:56.630
Then, Le...

00:19:56.630 --> 00:19:58.930
No, I'll do it.

00:19:58.930 --> 00:20:00.180
Scary.

00:20:00.180 --> 00:20:02.890
The leader is loved way too much in this group.

00:20:09.190 --> 00:20:10.560
Someone help me!

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:12.440
I can't possibly do this!

00:20:12.440 --> 00:20:15.110
Don't act like the heroine.

00:20:17.450 --> 00:20:20.780
Heh, you're a guy after all. I can count on you!

00:20:20.780 --> 00:20:25.450
Don't try the big-sisterly position
after giving up the heroine act.

00:20:25.450 --> 00:20:27.370
Come on, let's carry this.

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:44.680
It fit through pretty easily.

00:20:46.100 --> 00:20:49.650
How about we put this on the table
for now and inspect it?

00:20:49.650 --> 00:20:53.980
What do you think
about taking it apart into pieces?

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:58.280
But we just figured out
that we can bring this in as is.

00:20:58.280 --> 00:21:02.490
But if we take it apart,
we might figure something out.

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:08.910
As an artist, he can't just watch
the destruction of someone else's work.

00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:12.170
Then don't tell me, but tell Mr. Bare-Legs!

00:21:12.170 --> 00:21:15.960
He's the one who'll most likely
be happy to destroy it.

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:17.210
I see.

00:21:17.210 --> 00:21:20.930
If so, I guess today's discussion
has come to an end.

00:21:20.930 --> 00:21:26.100
I don't want this issue to take too long,
so let's all gather early tomorrow morning.

00:21:26.100 --> 00:21:30.940
Everyone aside from Nagahiro
must bring forth a beautiful theory.

00:21:30.940 --> 00:21:36.190
How did Kodaki Kawaike
bring that giant <i>hagoita </i>into this room?

00:21:36.190 --> 00:21:41.950
Oh, and please think about requests
for where you want to go for the training camp.

00:21:41.950 --> 00:21:44.450
And with that, we're disbanding for today!

00:21:44.530 --> 00:21:46.990
EPISODE 08

00:21:44.530 --> 00:21:46.990
THE PRETTY BOY TRAVELING
WITH THE BROCADE PORTRAIT

00:21:44.530 --> 00:21:46.990
PART 1

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:30.760
Such an uncomely posture.

00:23:28.510 --> 00:23:29.010
REUNION WITH THE DEVIL

00:23:32.390 --> 00:23:33.390
KODAKI
KAWAIKE

00:23:33.430 --> 00:23:35.520
Maidservant.
